{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790380873,"nonce":"eotckR2N+Vr201Ovu7nz0KxY+/E=","title":"TestInt64.testIncrement hits an unconditional Cranelift trap after unrelated edits to the file","message":"The staged TestInt64 conformance row passes (CONFORMANCE_OK 269), but a copy of it with an unrelated edit -- either a helper method added to TestInt64 (`function tl(n:Int, v:Bool)`) that wraps `t`, or a static counter added to the harness's `unit.Test.t` -- crashes with SIGILL in `unit.TestInt64.testIncrement [Cranelift] +0x48c`.\n\nRAYZOR_DUMP_CLIF=testIncrement shows the block after an `a == b` comparison on Int64 values (the `f(a == b)` sequence) ending in:\n\n    block87(v236: i8):\n        jump block96\n    block96:\n        trap user1\n\ni.e. a continuation block with no instructions or terminator of its own (MIR `Unreachable`), which Cranelift emits as a trap. Observed on a build at 32559426 plus uncommitted batch changes (virtual-dispatch defaults, Dynamic ++, reflect fixes, interface method values), with and WITHOUT the inliner parameter-retyping change -- so not caused by that change. Not yet checked on a clean HEAD build.\n\nReproducer: copy $TMPDIR/rayzor_conformance/run/TestInt64 (and its shared class path), add the `tl` helper to TestInt64, run with --release --no-cache --preset application.","files":null}]}